From 5b9778ba4b0056797453fbea6b10b73ddb6dd14f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:56:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/24] Withdraw a condemned incarnation's page claims from the
 quarantine

On the first 27.2 regression boot of this build the wire guard condemned
mid=2 at 18.47 s, and the guest later handed its pages to new window and
display surfaces (mid=9, 17, 18). Each MAP collided with mid=2, and the
quarantine held both sides, so the legitimate new surfaces were never
written and the desktop came out corrupted.

The guard's condemnation is protocol-independent evidence about the old
side alone: its own wire counts, read through a layout checked against
the kernel, dropped below what MAP saw while it was still mapped. That
incarnation now withdraws its page claims, at the worker's next tick,
in this order: it is quarantined (every page proof void, every CPU,
import and direct write refused), GPU writes already submitted to its
pages are waited for, its owed frame is dropped, and only then do
collision checks stop counting it as an owner. It is never restored; an
UNMAP ends it and a new MappingInternal for the id is a different
incarnation that inherits nothing. A debt armed for it later is dropped
at payment rather than put back.

A new mapping over its pages is then checked as any other, against every
remaining owner (surface_quarantine_resolved reason=owner_condemned
order=condemned_first). A mapping already quarantined because of it
loses exactly that partner; if none is left it is re-resolved, checked
against every other owner and its own wire counts read positive before
it is freed with its owed frame intact (order=collision_first), and
otherwise it stays held (surface_quarantine_kept / _partner_withdrawn).
Without that evidence, guard off or no anomaly, both sides of a
collision stay quarantined as before.

Tests: a new mapping over a withdrawn owner's pages is written; a third
valid owner still blocks it; a withdrawn incarnation whose count turns
positive stays refused and its debt is dropped; a new incarnation of the
old id is a valid owner again and is written; writes in flight to the
old pages settle before it is excluded, and the reverse order frees the
new side only after that; without wire evidence both stay quarantined.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
